# QA before handoff

Before telling the user work is ready to commit (or drafting commit messages as a handoff), **run that repo’s QA and fix failures**. Do not leave this to the pre-commit hook.

## webhemi-php

1. `composer fix` (if style/rector likely dirty)
2. `composer run qa` (same suite as `.githooks/pre-commit`)
3. Fix until green; re-stage auto-fixed files (`phpcbf` / cs-fixer / rector)
4. Never stage Windows `*:Zone.Identifier` junk

## webhemi-ui

At minimum before handoff:

1. `npm run typecheck`
2. `npm run lint`

Prefer `make test ui` when Chromatic token / full Storybook Vitest is available.

## Hub docs-only

No PHP/UI QA required for pure `docs/plan/` edits.
